window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Audible presents <i>Desi Down Under</i>, an Audible Original starring Prajakta Koli, Adarsh Gourav, and Taaruk Raina. Packed with adventure, romance, and comedy, <i>Desi Down Under</i> follows childhood best friends Devan (Adarsh Gourav), Meenu (Prajakta Koli), and Meenu's party animal twin brother Rahul (Taaruk Raina) as they go on their first trip abroad, training as lifesavers at the stunning Coogee beach in Sydney, Australia.</p> <p>Devan is determined to overcome death-defying trials in the shark-infested Sydney surf to earn his Bronze Medallion in lifesaving, so he can bring these lifesaving skills home and make his fishing community in Mangalore safer. Luckily Devan’s got his super driven bestie Meenu by his side. They're inseparable and both secretly have a huge crush on each other. They just don’t know how to tell each other!</p> <p>Meenu is a rebel who, despite her conservative parents' wishes for her to have a \"regular career\", finds her calling in Sydney on the waves. Meenu's twin brother, Rahul, who came on the trip as a chaperone for Meenu, is ready to date, party, and enjoy Sydney's queer dating scene to the max. No one can stop his wild antics, or help him as he faces one of the scariest experiences of all: falling in love. The trio’s conflicting goals in Australia become a real issue when their coach Shaunie reveals they all need to work together and qualify as a team to earn the Bronze Medallion. That’s right - if one of them doesn’t succeed, all three of them fail.</p> <p><i>Desi Down Under</i> is written and created by Indian-Aussie screenwriter Mithila Gupta, based on an idea by Mithila Gupta and Mala Sujan, directed by Mantra and produced by MnM Talkies.</p> <p>Disclaimer: This show contains expletives, strong language, and mature content for Adult listeners, including intimate scenes that support the storyline. This is a work of fiction and any resemblance to real persons, businesses, places, or events is coincidental. Any form of drugs, tobacco, and alcohol consumption are recorded for the sole purpose of the creation of the show. None of the actors support/promote consumption of drugs, tobacco, or alcohol. This show is not intended to offend or defame any individual, entity, caste, community, race, or religion, or to denigrate any institution or person, living or dead, and does not intend to outrage/insult or defame any religious sentiments, beliefs, or feelings of any person, entity, class, or community. Listener discretion is strongly advised.</p>"; 
